course: dictionary
lesson: 15352
title: Solidify: from liquid to solid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solidify is a verb. Its simplest meaning is to become solid, or to make something become solid. This usually happens when a liquid cools or freezes and turns hard. You can see the word «solid» inside it, which is a clue.
explain: «Leave the melted wax to solidify before you touch it.» The wax starts as a runny liquid and goes hard as it cools. So solidify means to turn from liquid into solid.
explain: You can also solidify a plan, a friendship or an idea. «The two friends solidified their friendship by playing together every day.» Here nothing is turning hard. It means the friendship became firmer and more certain. Ask yourself: is the thing turning hard, or getting stronger and surer?
fact: Solidify means to become solid, or to make something become solid.
fact: Solidify is the opposite of melt: melting turns a solid into a liquid.
fact: Water solidifies into ice at 0 °C.
fact: Lava solidifies into rock as it cools.
fact: You can also solidify a plan or friendship, which means to make it firmer and more certain.
exercise: «Water solidifies into ice when it gets cold enough.» What does solidifies mean here? | *Becomes solid | Evaporates into the air | Melts into a puddle | Floats on the top
exercise: «The lava slowly solidified into rock.» What did the lava turn into? | *Rock | Water | Dust | Gas
exercise: Mia wants to solidify her plan for the school trip. What does she want to do? | *Make the plan firmer and more certain | Melt the plan | Forget the plan | Throw the plan away
test: Which word is the opposite of solidify? | Set | Harden | Freeze | *Melt
test: «They wanted to solidify their friendship.» What does solidify mean here? | *Make it firmer and more certain | Make it melt | Forget about it | Break it apart
exam: «After an hour in the freezer, the jelly had solidified.» What has happened to the jelly? | *It has become solid | It has turned into a gas | It has melted | It has disappeared
